---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Review & testing methodology" description="How BotPlanet evaluates robots and labels its evidence.">
  <h1>Review & testing methodology</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="max-width:680px;">We are transparent about which conclusions are hands-on and which are researched.</p>

  <h2>Evidence levels</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Label</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="pill class">Tested</span></td><td>BotPlanet used the product hands-on and captured original evidence.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pill class">Hands-on demo</span></td><td>We saw a live demonstration, clearly identified as such.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pill class">Researched</span></td><td>Original analysis of specs, manuals, warranty, support and suitability.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pill class">Verified owner</span></td><td>Attributable evidence from a verified owner.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="pill class">Manufacturer claimed</span></td><td>A manufacturer claim we haven't independently verified.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>What we assess</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Suitability by pool type, size and cleaning need.</li>
    <li>Cleaning coverage: floor, walls, waterline, surface.</li>
    <li>Power (cordless vs corded), warranty, support and returns.</li>
    <li>Real limitations and who should avoid the product.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="note">At launch, our evidence is primarily "researched". We label everything honestly and upgrade to hands-on evidence as we obtain review units.</p>
</Base>
